            <ArticleTitle>A review of the incidence of pain after an operation treatment visit: Part I.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>224-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review presented some typically encountered painful sequellae from routine restorative dental treatment. A brief description of the importance of Tomes' processes and free nerve endings were mentioned also. This review should serve as a background for a clinical study concerning posttreatment pain that will be described in a later article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
